// Every path that decides an integer literal's type admits `u64`'s range
// (MISSING-x8Wq3): a `const`'s declared type, a call argument against the
// parameter's type, a `fun`'s return type, and a written type on a binding.
//
// The `i64` minimum is in here because it is spelled as its magnitude under a
// sign: the magnitude is 2^63, which only the widened literal can carry, so the
// minimum was unwritable too and is the signed half of the same rule.
const MASK: u64 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

fun take(x: u64).return: u64 = x

fun give().return: u64 = 18446744073709551615

fun main() {
    print(MASK)
    print(take(0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF))
    print(give())
    val min: i64 = -9223372036854775808
    print(min)
}
